      src/acceptance/execution/sandbox.py#0

  network-access-blocked-for-tests
    [scope_too_narrow] network-access-blocked-for-tests/loopback-connections-allowed
      The network block only refuses socket families outside `_ALLOWED_FAMILIES`, and `_ALLOWED_FAMILIES` contains `AF_UNIX` only. That leaves IPv4/IPv6 loopback and any other non-UNIX socket family unblocked if the test uses `socket.socket.connect` or `connect_ex` on them.
      src/acceptance/execution/netblock.py#0
    [scope_too_narrow] network-access-blocked-for-tests/direct-socket-apis-not-patched
      The plugin patches `socket.socket.connect`, `socket.socket.connect_ex`, `socket.getaddrinfo`, and `socket.create_connection`, but it does not intercept other network entry points such as `socket.socket.sendto`, `socket.socket.bind`, or lower-level libraries that open connections without those calls. A test using one of those paths could still reach the network.
      src/acceptance/execution/netblock.py#0
    [other] network-access-blocked-for-tests/c-extension-network-escape
      The block is only at the Python `socket` layer, so a C extension or other native code that opens or uses sockets without going through the patched Python functions can still make network connections during the run.
      src/acceptance/execution/netblock.py#0

